# Template: `make pi-install-udev` fills in @PI_LIBRARY_UUID@ and @MOUNT_UNIT@ (.deploy.env).
#
# Bring the audiobook library drive (and with it else-wer) back after a USB drop.
#
# On a Pi Zero 2 W everything hangs off a single dwc_otg root port: the library
# drive and a USB ethernet adapter can share one hub. A hub reset re-enumerates both,
# systemd unmounts the library mount, and else-wer.service is stopped along with it
# (it has RequiresMountsFor= on that mount).
#
# The kernel re-attaches the disk on its own, but nothing then mounts it:
#   - fstab uses `nofail`, so no boot target wants the mount unit at runtime, and
#   - a filesystem that reappears outside a systemd job only gets *marked* active,
#     which does not run the mount's dependencies.
# So the mount's WantedBy never fires and else-wer stays down until someone logs in.
#
# Matching the filesystem UUID (not /dev/sda1 — the kernel name is not stable across
# re-enumeration) makes the device unit want the mount, so the mount runs as a real
# job. That pulls in else-wer via WantedBy= on the mount unit in else-wer.service.
ACTION=="add|change", SUBSYSTEM=="block", ENV{ID_FS_UUID}=="@PI_LIBRARY_UUID@", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="@MOUNT_UNIT@"
